{"name":"Temptress","hex":"#3c2126","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"temptress","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alluring woman who seduces or exploits men.","A woman considered sexually attractive by men."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/temptress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Temptation","blocks":[{"text":"Temptation is a desire to engage in short-term urges for enjoyment that threatens long-term goals. \nIn the context of some religions, temptation is the inclination to sin. Temptation also describes the coaxing or inducing a person into committing such an act, by manipulation or otherwise of curiosity, desire or fear of loss something important to a person."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/William_Blake_Eve_Tempted_by_the_Serpent.jpg/330px-William_Blake_Eve_Tempted_by_the_Serpent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temptation"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/1280px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png/500px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-_Temptation_%281880%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Temptation, by William-Adolphe Bouguereau.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilliam-Adolphe_Bouguereau_(1825-19